WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:09.420
London - it’s easy to recognise…

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.389
but look closely at a map

00:00:11.389 --> 00:00:15.639
In the very centre there’s a one square mile
cut out

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.500
This is The City of London which lives in
a city named London

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.300
The City has its own mayor, laws, and police
force. In fact it behaves more like a separate

00:00:32.309 --> 00:00:34.899
country within the United Kingdom

00:00:34.899 --> 00:00:38.309
This is because The City’s been around for
much longer than than the UK

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:40.899
It was built by the Romans.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.260
And has remained semi-autonomous even since

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.519
To embody its fiery independence, the city’s
emblem is a dragon… not a bad choice

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.680
You’ll spot these statues - they guard the
boundary of the Square Mile

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.760
Nowadays The City is arguably the financial
capital of the world

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.340
And London is the world's biggest foreign
exchange market

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.000
But The City has a tiny residential
population

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.380
Every weekday workers flood into the banks,
law firms and offices which fill the Square Mile

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.700
But it’s not all work. This is 1pm

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:34.480
You might say no surprise here, City work’s having a
drink, but attitudes are changing

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.340
The legendary long lunch at the pub is now
seen as a bit of a macho relic

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.580
In 2017 Lloyd's of London, the legendary insurance
market, told it’s employees the party was over

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.820
No more drink during office hours

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:53.590
But, as you can see, not everyone got the
memo

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:58.100
Because here’s the rub of it, The City had
a reputation… when the after work crowd

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.790
go home, the place becomes a ghost town

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:06.580
But that is changing and leading are some
high flying dining spots

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.560
Sitting on top the Heron Tower is the duck
and waffle

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.540
it offers 24/7 service with a hell
of a view

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.900
This is about as refined as
a 24 hour waffle house gets

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:27.760
But the most talked about new guest, who’s
reinventing The City’s reputation, is call The Ned

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:32.870
Over 500 million pounds has been spent turning
this old bank into a private members club

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:34.170
and hotel

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:39.120
With 8 restaurants in the lobby and a bar
that stay open till 4am - The Ned has injected

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.440
some late night atmosphere into The City

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.520
This is after all the oldest part of London.
And following an injection of fun and flavour

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:53.430
it’s throwing down a
challenge to the rest of the city and shaking

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.860
off its stuffy reputation

